claims.claim:
Decode prerequisites before prefill can send:
- decode handshake reaches WaitingForInput and sets bootstrap_done;
- pop_preallocated admits the request against the metadata buffer, req_to_token slots and token budget, FIFO with break on the first failure;
- _send_kv_metadata/send_metadata pushes kv page indices, aux index, state indices and decode_prefix_len over zmq to every prefill rank.
The prefill bootstrap_thread stores the TransferInfo and sets WaitingForInput once all required_dst_info_num infos have arrived.

experiments.change:
Mount a conn.py variant that logs per TransferKVChunk:
- enqueue ts and shard_idx in add_transfer_request, plus queue length at put;
- dequeue ts in transfer_worker;
- time spent in wait_event.synchronize();
- duration of each _transfer_data / batch_transfer_sync call, with len(transfer_blocks) and bytes;
- is_last_chunk, room, worker_index.
Also log every decode session id and its port % QUEUE_SIZE.

conclusions_so_far:
HIP transport behaviour:
- one hipMemcpyAsync per request block, with no slicing;
- streams are picked round-robin from a 64-stream pool;
- submit returns only after a serial hipEventSynchronize on every event (hip_transport.cpp:479-511,535-591,631-653).
Per-block CPU costs: hipPointerGetAttributes, hipSetDevice, and two linear buffer scans (hip_transport.cpp:196-252,759-764; multi_transport.cpp:506-522).

machine_checks:
Standalone HIP-IPC copy microbenchmark inside the image, before any engine run (about 30 min, no sglang). Use mooncake TransferEngine batch_transfer_sync_write with the same env as the run (MC_TE_FILTERS, hip) and copy GPU0->GPU4 about 7 GB. Vary:
- block count: 1 / 1e3 / 1e4 / 1e5;
- caller threads: 1 / 4;
- sources: 4 GPUs (0-3 -> 4-7) at once;
- MC_HIP_NUM_STREAMS: 16 / 64 / 256.
Record GB/s and wall time per call. If the python TE path cannot be set up, fall back to a plain torch peer copy (`tensor.to('cuda:4')`) between the same GPU pairs for raw XGMI bandwidth only.
